From: deepak1556 <hop2deep@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 23:14:34 +0900
Subject: [profiler] Rebuild merged native associations for each snapshot

Native objects can be replaced while their JavaScript wrapper survives.
For example, Blink reuses a JSGlobalProxy across navigation, clearing its
association with the old DOMWindow and binding it to the new one.

HeapObjectsMap retains merged_native_entries_map_ across snapshots.
Adding the replacement native object therefore leaves two native
addresses pointing to the same wrapper entry. RemoveDeadEntries() builds
a reverse map keyed by entry index and assumes this mapping is unique,
triggering DCHECK(result.second).

This was observed when taking renderer heap snapshots before and after
reloads in the same Electron renderer isolate. Diagnostic logging showed
the following cppgc header addresses associated with one JSGlobalProxy:

  Snapshot   Native Window     Wrapper address   Snapshot ID
  Initial    0x1040203f028      0x3150102f434     90415
  Reload 1   0x10402155840      0x3150102f434     90415
  Reload 2   0x1040203b148      0x3150102f434     90415
  Reload 3   0x1040215f610      0x3150102f434     90415

All four associations were labeled:
  cpp=Window js=global [JSGlobalProxy]

The original failure was:
  Debug check failed: result.second.
    v8::internal::HeapObjectsMap::RemoveDeadEntries()
    v8::internal::HeapProfiler::TakeSnapshot(...)
    v8::HeapProfiler::TakeHeapSnapshot(...)

Clear merged native associations before rebuilding the native graph for
each snapshot. This removes stale native addresses while preserving the
existing JavaScript object IDs. Rebuild both cppgc and embedder graph
associations through their existing traversal paths.

Upstreamed at https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8369219.

diff --git a/src/profiler/heap-snapshot-generator.cc b/src/profiler/heap-snapshot-generator.cc
index 6681d711108a51e021e0ffa5ef22048f865c47be..7b2bcee6affcbfcba03939293862e272936efacc 100644
--- a/src/profiler/heap-snapshot-generator.cc
+++ b/src/profiler/heap-snapshot-generator.cc
@@ -787,6 +787,10 @@ void HeapObjectsMap::AddMergedNativeEntry(NativeObject addr,
   }
 }
 
+void HeapObjectsMap::ClearMergedNativeEntries() {
+  merged_native_entries_map_.clear();
+}
+
 void HeapObjectsMap::StopHeapObjectsTracking() { time_intervals_.clear(); }
 
 void HeapObjectsMap::UpdateHeapObjectsMap() {
@@ -3575,6 +3579,11 @@ bool NativeObjectsExplorer::IterateAndExtractReferences(
   DisallowGarbageCollection no_gc;
   HandleScope scope(isolate_);
 
+  // Native objects can be replaced while their JS wrapper survives.
+  // Rebuild these associations each snapshot instead of retaining
+  // stale native addresses for live wrapper entries.
+  heap_object_map_->ClearMergedNativeEntries();
+
   if (isolate_->heap()->cpp_heap()) {
     CppGraphBuilder::Run(
         v8::internal::CppHeap::From(isolate_->heap()->cpp_heap()), generator_,
